::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: guard-kinds fixture ]

One rule per guard spelling, so the listing has all four to render and
one dead pointer to report.

==[ crate-layering ]

@rule(crate-layering){
  guard: { twrit: layers }

  layers: {
    0: list("thing")
  }
}

==[ generated-md-not-edited ]

@rule(generated-md-not-edited){
  guard: { runs: "just docs-check" }
}

==[ no-vocabulary ]

@rule(no-vocabulary){
  guard: { test: "tests/src/present.rs" }
}

==[ renamed-away ]

@rule(renamed-away){
  guard: { test: "tests/src/gone.rs" }
}

The test this points at does not exist. Nothing runs it, and nothing
would have said so.

==[ blueprint-shape ]

@rule(blueprint-shape){
  guard: { none: "no cheap check for the args shape yet" }
}
